      "dataStream": "Prompt Template\rFill in the sections below. The clearer the role, the context and the expected format, the better the answer — and the easier it is to reuse the prompt later.\rRole\rWho the AI should be when answering. E.g. a demanding technical reviewer, a patient teacher, a lawyer specialised in contracts.\rContext\rWhat it needs to know before starting: the project, the audience, what has been tried, what cannot change.\rTask\rWhat you want, in one direct sentence. One request per prompt usually beats five at once.\rAnswer format\rHow the answer should arrive: table, list, running text, how many words, in which language.\rConstraints\rWhat to avoid: jargon, unsourced assumptions, changing what is already decided, going over a length.\rExample of what I expect\rA short example of the result you want. It improves the answer the most — and is the thing people most often forget to write.\rFinal prompt\r\r\n",
